@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# WIP packed ordinary filter checkpoint
+
+This is an experimental, unvalidated hypothesis branch from exact selected9d `9d64b7c53ddaea7a578d247ebd28db43ae0d4e56`. Work stopped at Onyr's request. The implementation is not ready for routing experiments, promotion or performance interpretation. No remote action, reservation or routing run was performed. Existing a2dc/7d profiler worktrees, artifacts and frozen helpers were not edited.
+
+The branch is `proof-speed/packed-ordinary-filter`, in `$WORKSPACE/kayros-proof-packed-ordinary-filter`. The implementation contract is `kayros-ablation/outputs/ms58/dabia-20261110/u-filter-opportunity-gros-v1/analysis/dominance-index-20261110T113021Z/assessment.md`. Astra reviewed the design and supplied allocation-failure, ABI and maintenance requirements. Actual source/fixture review by `dominance_index_astra` remains pending.
+
+## Current implementation
+
+The default-OFF public CMake flag `KAYROS_PACKED_ORDINARY_FILTER` enables a sidecar keyed by `(vertex, existing demand key)`. Rows own copied `VertexSet U` and `double min_cost`, with no label or relocating bucket pointers. The initial threshold is 64. Ordinary queries use rows only with partial dominance, cost sorting and unrelaxed U checks. Missing metadata retains scalar fallback. Eligible processed insertion creates a cache. An existing invalid cache can rebuild lazily on a later eligible query.
+
+Sorted insertion captures the iterator from the original `insert_sorted` and mirrors its exact position. Fallback-mode insertions and retirements maintain any valid cache. Partial correction refreshes the copied double immediately and unconditionally after recomputation, including equal values and signed zero. Retirement erases the matching row before the original pointer erase. The existing correction stable sort invalidates row order. Cleanup and `SetProblem` clear metadata. The survivor theta/PWL/trace body remains shared and unchanged.
+
+The packed loop evaluates the same epsilon cost predicate before the same subset predicate, then loads the label pointer for survivors. Label ownership and ILS source are untouched. Optional cache allocations catch only `std::bad_alloc`, discard all metadata and suppress rebuilding until `Clean`. A diagnostic allocation-failure injector exists only with the separate metrics flag.
+
+`KAYROS_PACKED_ORDINARY_FILTER_METRICS` is separately default OFF and PUBLIC. It records logical insertion/erasure shift bytes, rows built, refreshes, aggregate live/capacity payload and peaks, allocation failures, query visits, subset tests and survivor dereferences. It also records native query traces. This mode perturbs timings and is unsuitable for performance measurements. Container/node overhead and allocator traffic are not measured. Debug builds additionally verify rows and must not be used for timing.
+
+## Completed checks
+
+- C++23 syntax checks of candidate monodirectional and bidirectional sources passed in the project Nix shell.
+- An isolated candidate CPLEX metrics build completed `lera`, `_lera` and `_core`.
+- A separate baseline source archive of exact9d was extracted under the candidate's ignored `build/packed-base-source`, and its isolated CPLEX build completed the same targets. The selected9d worktree was not used as a build directory or edited.
+- Candidate flag-OFF preprocessing matched exact9d for the 7 checked source/header streams, including the bridge. Log `/tmp/packed-off-equivalence.log` contains token hashes.
+- Local baseline and candidate `_core` binaries have the same SHA-256, `da8a6d475579c6ab403f51d74b054bebd8be628ce7614d105396c1d8a1c02e4b`.
+- `git diff --check` passed at checkpoint.
+
+## Known failure and validation status
+
+The newly written full-state native fixture did not compile in either matching build. Both compilers report `tests/cpp/test_packed_ordinary_filter.cpp:76:18: error: 'min' was not declared in this scope`. The immediate likely correction is qualifying the existing interval minimum call as `std::min(img(l.duration))`, matching the original correction fixture. This was deliberately left unfixed because work was stopped. No fixture assertions have run and no state digest or semantic equivalence has been established.
+
